The LOG command is used to get a current list of the users of the BBS.
When you enter the command, you will be prompted:

List (A)ll or (S)earch for a pattern?

If you want a complete listing, enter 'A'.  If you have an idea as to the
user(s) you are looking for, select 'S'.  You must then supply a pattern of
letters.  If the pattern is found in the handles of any users, those users
will be displayed.
